#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:100
msgid "Standalone image methods removed *(major)*"
msgstr "Méthodes d'image autonomes supprimées *(majeur)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:102
msgid ""
":class:`image.threshold`, ``image.centroid()``, "
"``image.orientation_radians()``, ``image.orientation_degrees()``, and "
"``image.pixels()`` were removed. The centroid / orientation / pixel-count "
"data is now available as fields of the blob tuples returned by "
"``find_blobs()``."
msgstr ""
":class:`image.threshold`, ``image.centroid()``, "
"``image.orientation_radians()``, ``image.orientation_degrees()`` et "
"``image.pixels()`` ont été supprimées. Les données de centroïde / "
"orientation / nombre de pixels sont désormais disponibles sous forme de "
"champs des tuples de blob retournés par ``find_blobs()``."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:107
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `9e5d379c1 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/9e5d379c1>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `9e5d379c1 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/9e5d379c1>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:112
msgid "Imlib method renames *(major)*"
msgstr "Renommages de méthodes imlib *(majeur)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:114
msgid ""
"Several image methods were renamed/reworked: ``image.subimg()`` → "
"``image.copy()``, ``image.blit()`` → ``image.replace()``, and "
"``image.blend()`` was changed to match the other two-image ops. The "
"``image.scale()`` / ``scaled()`` / ``rainbow()`` methods were removed "
"(``rainbow`` moved to the FIR module). Update calls to the new names."
msgstr ""
"Plusieurs méthodes d'image ont été renommées/retravaillées : "
"``image.subimg()`` → ``image.copy()``, ``image.blit()`` → "
"``image.replace()``, et ``image.blend()`` a été modifiée pour correspondre "
"aux deux autres opérations sur deux images. Les méthodes ``image.scale()`` /"
" ``scaled()`` / ``rainbow()`` ont été supprimées (``rainbow`` a été déplacée"
" vers le module FIR). Mettez à jour les appels avec les nouveaux noms."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:120
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `b534dc6ff <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/b534dc6ff>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `b534dc6ff "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/b534dc6ff>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:125
msgid "``find_eyes()`` renamed to ``find_eye()`` *(minor)*"
msgstr "``find_eyes()`` renommée en ``find_eye()`` *(mineur)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:127
msgid ""
"``image.find_eyes()`` was renamed to ``image.find_eye()`` and now returns a "
"2-tuple iris ``(x, y)`` instead of the previous eyes tuple. Rename the call "
"and update the return handling."
msgstr ""
"``image.find_eyes()`` a été renommée en ``image.find_eye()`` et retourne "
"désormais un 2-tuple d'iris ``(x, y)`` au lieu de l'ancien tuple d'yeux. "
"Renommez l'appel et mettez à jour la gestion de la valeur de retour."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:131
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `7a01a9bed <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/7a01a9bed>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `7a01a9bed "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/7a01a9bed>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:136
msgid "``image.compress()`` renamed to ``compressed()`` *(minor)*"
msgstr "``image.compress()`` renommée en ``compressed()`` *(mineur)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:138
msgid ""
"``image.compress()`` (which returned a new JPEG image) was renamed to "
"``image.compressed()``; the new ``image.compress()`` instead compresses the "
"image in place and returns ``None``. ``image.save()`` also gained a "
"``quality=`` keyword and now returns ``None`` instead of ``True``. Migrate "
"``img.compress(q)`` (expecting a returned image) to "
"``img.compressed(quality=q)``."
msgstr ""
"``image.compress()`` (qui retournait une nouvelle image JPEG) a été renommée"
" en ``image.compressed()`` ; le nouveau ``image.compress()`` compresse "
"plutôt l'image sur place et retourne ``None``. ``image.save()`` a également "
"reçu un argument nommé ``quality=`` et retourne désormais ``None`` au lieu "
"de ``True``. Migrez ``img.compress(q)`` (qui attend une image retournée) "
"vers ``img.compressed(quality=q)``."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v1.4.0.rst:145
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `367e5fdd3 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/367e5fdd3>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits :* `367e5fdd3 "
"<https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/367e5fdd3>`__"

